WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:01.479
What about Miley Cyclops?

00:00:01.479 --> 00:00:02.479
Damn it.

00:00:02.479 --> 00:00:03.479
That's good.

00:00:03.479 --> 00:00:04.700
I don't hate it.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.330
She can shoot laser beams out of her eyes.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:09.330
Shoots rays.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.860
Billy Rays.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:17.600
Tom, what are some forgotten Marvel superheroes
that you think deserve to be in the MCU?

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:21.730
I was kind of excited about this one.

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.720
So I think one of the big complaints that's
sort of been coming in about the MCU the last

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.250
few years has been just kind of the general
bloodlessness of it.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:33.040
That was something that came up in a lot of
reviews for Black Widow, especially.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.350
You've got the right, the scene where Florence
Pugh is explosion-proof.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:42.360
She stabbed someone in the stomach and they're
like, "Oh!"

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:46.160
And then, she dies, but there's no blood.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.160
Yeah.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.160
Yeah.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:54.620
As a general rule, anybody whose contract
isn't up is still going to be around by the

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.540
time that the credits roll.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:03.080
There was this immensely bleak comic back
in the Eighties called Strikeforce: Morituri.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.479
Have you ever heard of that?

00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:06.479
No.

00:01:06.479 --> 00:01:09.009
It is grim.

00:01:09.009 --> 00:01:10.009
It was a Marvel comic.

00:01:10.009 --> 00:01:11.170
It ran for a couple years back in the Eighties.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.409
I think it only lasted 31 issues.

00:01:14.409 --> 00:01:20.180
The concept is that Earth has been overrun
by aliens, and they're like these nasty ... It's

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.369
horrifying.

00:01:21.369 --> 00:01:24.470
They're popping the heads off of kids to establish
dominance.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:28.709
They're taking swaths of people up into the
upper atmosphere, and then releasing them

00:01:28.709 --> 00:01:31.609
down so that they burn up as they reenter.

00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:32.609
Jesus.

00:01:32.609 --> 00:01:35.450
Yeah, no, it's really dark.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:42.479
And then, this scientist comes up with this
kind of like last ditch attempt to maybe win

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:48.250
this war, and it's that he figures out a process
that gives people superpowers.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.579
But the problem is that it only works on about
5% of people.

00:01:51.579 --> 00:01:54.819
They got to be pretty young for it to work.

00:01:54.819 --> 00:01:59.490
And, and if you do go through the process,
the stress that it puts on your body is going

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.460
to kill you within a year.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:05.439
So it's this group of superpowered people
who know that whether they win this war or

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:07.549
not, they're going to die.

00:02:07.549 --> 00:02:09.670
Oh my God.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:10.670
Immensely grim.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:13.410
Yeah, no, it's so dark.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:17.660
Obviously, it wouldn't necessarily work within
like the MCU proper, but with them doing all

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:21.850
of the alternate universes, and the What Ifs,
and the different timelines, I don't know.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:25.640
It could be kind of a cool standalone thing.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:26.640
I don't know.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.170
It would be interesting to see a story where
you don't know if the good guys are going

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.040
to win or not on a week-to-week basis.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:37.650
It's sort of just a constant Ned Stark getting
killed at the end of the first season of Game

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.790
of Thrones, but just every week.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:40.790
You never know.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:43.750
Plus, you could probably get in a bunch of
great actors to do it if they know that they're

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:48.570
not devoting the next 10 years of their lives
to this one project that they got to keep

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.830
doing over and over again.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.720
You said that they have to be young, though.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.360
That's my question, could you hire any actor
to do it?

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.950
Could you play around with the age thing?

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.320
How young do they have to be?

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.950
So in the comics, the ideal age is 18 to 21.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:04.950
Oh, cool.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:05.950
Okay.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:10.700
But the thing is that, they can put older
people through it, but the process will kill

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:11.960
them faster.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:12.960
Oh.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.150
Yeah, it's a really dark story.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:20.580
So you could get a real A-lister in there
who's on the older side and be like, "Well,

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.760
you're just going to die really fast, so don't
worry about it."

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.760
Sure. Yeah.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:24.760
I don't know.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:25.615
I think that could be neat.

00:03:25.615 --> 00:03:26.615
Yeah.

00:03:26.615 --> 00:03:28.534
What's this called again?

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:30.935
Strikeforce: Morituri.

00:03:30.935 --> 00:03:38.110
Was there any kind of lasting ramifications
on the Marvel universe after it wrapped up?

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.110
Practically none.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:43.260
It got its own universe designation later
on down the line.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.940
I think they made a couple of references to
it the last few years, maybe.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:51.060
But yeah, no, it was just kind of thrown aside.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:56.200
And it's weird, yeah, I haven't seen anybody
write anything about it, the last few years.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.200
All right.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.569
But, cool, weird, dark concept.

00:03:59.569 --> 00:04:00.569
Definitely.

00:04:00.569 --> 00:04:04.600
Alternately, my second choice would be NFL
SuperPro, who was-

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.970
I know SuperPro.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.180
We all know SuperPro.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:15.521
Back in the Nineties, there was a brief and
beautiful period where ex-NFL superstar, Phil

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:22.740
Grayfield, who blew out his knee, had a sports
injury, became a sports reporter, was interviewing

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:30.779
a super scientist/NFL fan, and received a
set of indestructible football uniform clothes.

00:04:30.779 --> 00:04:34.020
Yeah, those exist.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:39.729
During the interview, criminals break in and
rob the place.

00:04:39.729 --> 00:04:44.780
And there's an explosion of science chemicals
and NFL memorabilia, which grant Phil Grayfield

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:49.530
the powers of the NFL SuperPro.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:53.319
And he uses his sports powers to stop sports
crimes.

00:04:53.319 --> 00:04:54.360
Right.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.889
Introduces a lot of great characters.

00:04:55.889 --> 00:05:00.960
You've got the super villains like Instant
Replay, who can travel in time just a little

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.139
bit.

00:05:02.139 --> 00:05:08.449
Issue 10, you get to meet a guy, his superhero
name is the Almighty Dollar.

00:05:08.449 --> 00:05:11.139
He gets the power to shoot pennies out of
his hands.

00:05:11.139 --> 00:05:14.310
Generally considered one of the worst comics
ever made.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:17.110
Wasn't it a tie-in?

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:20.120
Was it a licensing thing between Marvel and
the NFL?

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.120
It's half-and-half.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:24.080
Half of the reason they haven't used the character
again is because of the licensing thing, and

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.810
then half of the reason is that it's the worst
idea that anybody's ever had.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:30.529
A question; what's a sports crime?

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:32.409
What's a sports crime?

00:05:32.409 --> 00:05:34.759
Stealing the the Stanley Cup?

00:05:34.759 --> 00:05:38.969
I can't leave this conversation without knowing
what a sports crime is.

00:05:38.969 --> 00:05:41.289
You know, I'm not going to sit here and mansplain
sports crimes to you.

00:05:41.289 --> 00:05:44.409
I know about sports, but I don't what a sports
crime is.

00:05:44.409 --> 00:05:46.490
I think we all know what a sports crime is.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:47.490
Okay.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:48.490
I don't recall.

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:49.490
I'm telling you I don't know.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.490
Stealing first?

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:53.259
I don't know if you could ... You can't steal
first.

00:05:53.259 --> 00:05:57.029
I mean, that would be a crime.

00:05:57.029 --> 00:05:58.520
Stealing any base.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.309
Oh, in football.

00:06:01.309 --> 00:06:02.719
In football.

00:06:02.719 --> 00:06:03.999
Yep.

00:06:03.999 --> 00:06:06.400
Those are my picks.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.069
I'm sorry, any further questions about NFL
SuperPro?

00:06:08.069 --> 00:06:12.089
I was going to say, though, I mean, it's not
totally out of the picture, right, because

00:06:12.089 --> 00:06:15.610
Disney owns ESPN?

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:16.610
And therefore, football.

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:17.610
That's right, yeah.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:18.610
To a certain extent, yeah.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:21.969
I mean, there's room for it to come back.

00:06:21.969 --> 00:06:23.259
The sport of football.

00:06:23.259 --> 00:06:26.110
Because ESPN does air some NFL games.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:30.979
So maybe, as part of the rights package, next
time they renegotiate the project, they say-

00:06:30.979 --> 00:06:31.979
Or.

00:06:31.979 --> 00:06:32.979
... Yes?

00:06:32.979 --> 00:06:33.979
Maybe the next time, the Super Bowl's on ABC.

00:06:33.979 --> 00:06:36.419
They're like, "Let's bring him back."

00:06:36.419 --> 00:06:37.419
That's right.

00:06:37.419 --> 00:06:39.069
Halftime Show feature SuperPro.

00:06:39.069 --> 00:06:42.030
Javier Bardem as NFL SuperPro.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:44.569
The SuperPro Halftime Show.

00:06:44.569 --> 00:06:45.569
Yeah.

00:06:45.569 --> 00:06:46.569
All right.

00:06:46.569 --> 00:06:47.569
Oh, look at that.

00:06:47.569 --> 00:06:48.569
This thing writes itself.

00:06:48.569 --> 00:06:49.569
I mean, that was terrific.

00:06:49.569 --> 00:06:50.569
Come on, ABC, write us a check.

00:06:50.569 --> 00:06:51.569
Yeah.

00:06:51.569 --> 00:06:52.569
Yes, please.

00:06:52.569 --> 00:06:53.569
Finally.

00:06:53.569 --> 00:06:54.569
Finally.

00:06:54.569 --> 00:06:55.990
We have so many good ideas.

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:56.990
Okay.

00:06:56.990 --> 00:07:00.800
Nina, what are some forgotten Marvel heroes
that you think should be a part of the MCU?

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:05.069
Well, I only have the one, but I think it
comes with endless spinoff possibilities.

00:07:05.069 --> 00:07:06.069
One is plenty.

00:07:06.069 --> 00:07:07.069
I'm sure.

00:07:07.069 --> 00:07:08.069
Perfect.

00:07:08.069 --> 00:07:11.860
So in the 1990s, I believe the year was 1994?

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:17.699
Yes, it was a 1994 imprint through Marvel
called Marvel Music, and each issue was about

00:07:17.699 --> 00:07:19.389
a different actual musician.

00:07:19.389 --> 00:07:21.139
So they did The Rolling Stones.

00:07:21.139 --> 00:07:23.770
They did Bob Marley, Alice Cooper.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.689
And I'm not going to pick any of those because
those might be fun.

00:07:26.689 --> 00:07:34.580
I'm going to pick Billy Ray Cyrus, who is
technically, legally, somehow a Marvel character

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:37.860
because he has one comic book.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:43.240
So in this comic book, he rides around on
a horse a lot.

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:44.759
I think there's two distinct stories in it.

00:07:44.759 --> 00:07:46.020
I tried reading it.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.469
I couldn't get through it.

00:07:47.469 --> 00:07:49.509
It's pretty bad.

00:07:49.509 --> 00:07:53.479
At a certain point, I was like, "I have literally
a thousand better ways to spend my time."

00:07:53.479 --> 00:07:54.530
But, the first-

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:57.509
Give us a broad strokes synopsis here.

00:07:57.509 --> 00:07:59.139
What happens?

00:07:59.139 --> 00:08:05.199
In one story that we could now ever do, now,
it is him fighting the ghost of a Native American

00:08:05.199 --> 00:08:10.839
chief, using not the term Native American,
so problematic on a hundred different levels.

00:08:10.839 --> 00:08:15.280
But the second one is similar to my dream
What If...? story, where he rides through

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:19.689
some ... He gets on a mysterious bus or something,
and he ends up in the 13th century, and he

00:08:19.689 --> 00:08:20.689
has to slay a dragon.

00:08:20.689 --> 00:08:22.270
Billy Ray Cyrus does.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:25.559
Billy Ray Cyrus has to slay a dragon in the
13th century, yes.

00:08:25.559 --> 00:08:30.539
This is a real Marvel comic, where Billy Ray
Cyrus fights a dragon in the thirteenth century?

00:08:30.539 --> 00:08:31.539
That's correct.

00:08:31.539 --> 00:08:32.539
Yes.

00:08:32.539 --> 00:08:33.539
And like all of these start with-

00:08:33.539 --> 00:08:35.539
He has the Achy Breaky Heart of a hero, Brian.

00:08:35.539 --> 00:08:38.590
And all of these start with him walking around,
being Billy Ray, and people just run up to

00:08:38.590 --> 00:08:40.570
him, and are like, "Oh my God."

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:41.970
And then, something weird happens.

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:46.400
So there's a weird, separate thread where
he just has people constantly running up to

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:48.460
him on the street and losing their minds.

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:53.610
But the reason that I picked Billy Ray Cyrus
is, first of all, easy casting.

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.510
He can play himself.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.870
I mean, there's no dream casting here.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.860
If they can afford him.

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:00.860
True.

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:03.860
But, would this open the door for Miley Cyrus
to be in the Marvel Cinematic Universe?

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:04.860
Maybe.

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:08.840
And that's something I'd much rather ... She's
already in it?

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:10.130
She's already in somewhere.

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:11.720
Wait, was she?

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:13.230
Was she?

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.230
She totally is.

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:15.230
Yeah, man.

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:17.150
Guardians of the Galaxy 2, when you get to
meet the original, Ravagers, the original

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:19.090
Guardians of the Galaxy, she plays the-

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:20.090
Okay.

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:21.090
You're right.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:22.440
Well I'm saying has herself.

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:23.440
She does?

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.160
Yeah, dude.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.430
Miley Cyrus?

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:31.490
So there's the original Guardians team with
with Sylvester Stallone.

00:09:31.490 --> 00:09:34.590
There's like a robot head that you have talking
to them.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.000
I can't remember the character's name.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.940
Yeah, it's voiced by Miley Cyrus.

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:39.940
No.

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:40.940
Yeah.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:44.940
Michael Rosenbaum's in there as the crystal
guy.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:45.940
Yeah.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:46.940
All right.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:48.250
Well, Tom, you make a fair point, but I'm
saying I want her to be in the Marvel Cinematic

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.850
Universe as herself.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:50.850
As herself.

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:51.850
Yes.

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:55.900
As the daughter of Marvel character, Billy
Ray Cyrus.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:10:00.160
Do you think that there's any room in this
story for her to have an auxiliary personality

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:06.010
that she, I don't know, maybe like a secret
persona, with which she ... I don't know.

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:07.010
Sorry.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:10.370
I'm still reeling from the discovery that
Miley Cyrus is in Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:12.950
I think maybe, occasionally, she could wear
a wig and perform at pop concerts.

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:14.050
I'm not ruling anything out.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:15.300
Now that's an idea.

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.300
I know.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:17.300
We could do well with that.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:20.970
But no, I mean, Miley Cyrus, I love watching
her do just about anything.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:22.370
She's a very charismatic person.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:27.380
So let's get the Billy Ray thing out the way,
and then, all of a sudden, boom, Miley Cyrus

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:28.940
playing herself in the MCU.

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:29.940
I'm sorry.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.050
I didn't mean to jump on the fact that she
was already in there.

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:35.880
I just, I figured that the YouTube comments
are going to instantly fill up and didn't

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:37.620
want to let them beat us to the punch telling
us that we're wrong.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:38.620
No, No, it's distinct.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:39.620
You're right.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:40.620
It's distinct enough.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:41.620
She's not playing a robot head.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:45.770
She's playing potential alien human being
Miley Cyrus because she's got the Bowie alien,

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:48.520
maybe you're not from this planet kind of
vibe going.

00:10:48.520 --> 00:10:52.880
What would the name of her secret identity
be, if you had to make something up off the

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:53.880
top of your head?

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:57.220
I really didn't want you to ask me that because
I can't think of anything.

00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:00.090
I'm trying to think of a planet pun.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:06.870
Maybe like ... Got nothing.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.430
Jenny Jupiter.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.990
I think that one might be taken already.

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:13.510
We might need to check the copyright on that
one.

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:15.150
What about Miley Cyclops?

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.890
Damn it, that's good.

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:17.970
I don't hate it.

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.010
She can shoot laser beams out of her eyes.

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:22.510
Shoots rays.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:23.680
Billy Rays.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:25.040
Can you cut my terrible suggestion?

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:26.040
Thanks, editing team.

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:27.600
They're not going to cut it.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:28.600
Okay.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:31.870
I love this.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:33.090
Now, Brian.

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:34.090
Yes?

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:35.090
Talk to us.

